  "name": "Grant tracker",
  "publisher": "Initiative",
  "description": "Every application, its deadline, and what you owe the funder afterwards.",
  "long_description": "Each grant or appeal is a card that moves from Prospects to Writing to Submitted, then Awarded or Declined. Cards hold the funder, what you asked for, what you got, the deadline and when the report is due, because winning a grant is how you find out you have to write a report about it.\n\nThe deadline is the card's due date, so My Tasks and the calendar remind the right person in time. The amounts have no currency. Rename them if that bothers you.",
